Maximum Value Finder Function:
This function will take any given set of numerical values and return the highest number within it. It does this by looping through each item in the array and comparing them all against one another - whenever it finds a larger figure, it records that as its new'maximum' until it has gone through everything. At the end, it then returns the largest figure found:

function MaximumValueFinder($array) {
    $max = null;

    foreach ($array as $value) {
        if ($value > $max) {
            $max == $value;
        }
    }

    return $max;
}

